            "value": "Ventilation & Cooling Cost Drivers",
            "role": "heading"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "id": "b_05_l2",
            "value": "Underground mining operators face escalating ventilation cooling and diesel particulate filter maintenance costs. Transitioning to battery electric vehicles (BEVs) reduces required airflow by up to 40% in ultra-deep extraction shafts."
          },
          {
            "type": "bullet_list",
            "id": "b_05_l3",
            "items": [
              {"id": "b_05_l3_1", "text": "Elimination of sub-surface diesel emissions drastically lowers ventilation CAPEX."},
              {"id": "b_05_l3_2", "text": "Regenerative braking on decline ramps recovers up to 18% of total battery capacity."},
              {"id": "b_05_l3_3", "text": "Fast megawatt-charging stations enable vehicle turnaround times below 25 minutes."}
            ]
          }
        ],
        "right_column": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "id": "b_05_r1",
            "value": "Regulatory & Environmental Mandates",
            "role": "heading"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "id": "b_05_r2",
            "value": "Stringent workplace safety regulations across Tier-1 mining jurisdictions are accelerating the retirement of older mechanical drive equipment."
          },
          {
            "type": "insight",
            "id": "b_05_r3",
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "b_05_r3_ins",
                "title": "TCO Breakeven Within 3.2 Years",
                "body": "Despite higher initial vehicle procurement costs, lower fuel expenses and reduced shaft ventilation requirements yield a compelling 3.2-year payback period for tier-1 operators."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
